# School Lab — Project Overview

Multi-school management SaaS for private Brazilian schools. Product UI locale is `pt-BR`; repository language is English (see the `core/language-conventions` rule).

## Monorepo layout
- `web/` — Rails 8.1, API-only (`config.api_only = true`), serving the versioned REST API (single source of business rules). Stack is locked; see the `web/web-rails` rule.
- `frontend/main` — React + Vite SPA, the product web UI. Consumes the API; never duplicates business rules.
- `frontend/base` — upstream template the SPA started from. Reference only; not the product.
- `app/` — React Native mobile. Consumes the API; never duplicates business rules.
- `docs/` — anchor docs, PRDs, guidelines. Source of truth for scope. Human-facing engineering standards live in `docs/guidelines/`.

## Working convention
Follow the documented flow (`docs/product-map.md`): anchor docs → domain PRDs (`docs/prds/`) → modeling (narrative in `docs/modeling/`) + database (DBML/DER in `docs/database/`) → implementation in `web/`. Do not implement domains that lack a PRD without flagging it.

## `.cursor` layout
- `rules/core/` — cross-cutting, always-applied rules (this file, language, LGPD, branch naming).
- `rules/docs/`, `rules/web/`, `rules/app/` — scoped by surface via `globs`; the folder is organizational, activation is driven by frontmatter.
- `agents/` — specialized subagents (`rails-implementer` orchestrates; `migration-agent`, `policy-agent`, `service-agent`, `api-controller-agent` for `web/`; `prd-reviewer`, `doc-consistency-checker` for docs).
- `skills/` — grouped by context (`core/`, `docs/`, `web/`, `web-ui/`, `app/`).
- Detailed "why" for these rules lives in `docs/guidelines/`; rules stay terse and point there.

## Ground rules
- Business logic lives in the API layer (service objects), shared by web + mobile.
- Data is isolated per school (`school_id`); never leak data across schools.
- When unsure about scope, check `docs/open-questions.md` before assuming.
